<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Telinfo 1996 profit soars 74 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian Telinfo 1996 profit soars 74 pct.</headline>
<text>
<p>LEUVEN, Belgium, Jan 31, Reuter - Provisional full year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			  221   v  127</p>
<p>    Current profit			    290   v  275</p>
<p>    Operating profit			  326   v  369</p>
<p>    Cons turnover (billion)		 6.5   v  6.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Telinfo NV is a Belgian telephone and data communications company. It is 41 percent-owned by a consortium comprising Belgian steel maker Sidmar NV, a unit of Luxembourg's Arbed and the Cordier Group.  </p>
<p>    Cons cash flow			    506   v  637</p>
<p>    Own equity				1,953   v  n/c</p>
<p>    Gross dividend per share (francs)     8   v    0</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		   4,912   v  n/c</p>
<p>    Finacial debt			     980   v  n/c</p>
<p>    Group net per share (francs)	   41   v   33</p>
<p>NOTE - Telinfo said it would publish full 1996 figures after the annual general shareholders meeting on May 30. It said that the dividend would be payable from June 16.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
